      en: "Kloten is located in the canton of Zurich and is primarily known internationally as the site of Zurich Airport, which occupies a significant portion of the municipal area. The history of settlement in the area dates back to Roman times, with excavations revealing the remains of a former Roman villa. The first documentary mention occurred in 1155 under the name Clotun. For a long time, Kloten remained a rural village until the construction of the international airport in 1948 triggered a radical transformation. Today, the city functions as one of the most important transport hubs in Central Europe and houses numerous companies in the aviation and logistics sectors. Geographically, Kloten lies in the Glatt Valley at an altitude of approximately 446 meters above sea level. Despite the industrial influence of the airport, the city possesses extensive forested areas such as the Hardwald, which serve as local recreation zones. Urban planning in recent decades has focused heavily on managing the enormous volume of traffic and developing modern service centers.",
